From 04658cd8483f7e42b39924af40df56587f30acc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "prompt.ac/@jeffrey" <mail@aesthetic.computer>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:34:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] NELA Open Graph link previews

Outline v1.9.2 sends a <title> and description but no Open Graph tags,
so Signal, iMessage and Slack show "Outline" and the stock blurb for
every link.

- renderApp emits og:* and twitter:* tags on every page: site name from
  OG_SITE_NAME (APP_NAME is fixed and names the product in the UI),
  description from OG_DESCRIPTION (falling back to the stock text, no
  longer double-escaped), and a 1200x630 card image.
- /og/default.png draws the site card; /og/s/:shareId.png and
  /og/s/:shareId/doc/:documentSlug.png draw a card titled with the
  published document. Titles come only from loadPublicShare, so private
  documents never appear on a card; unknown shares get the site card.
- server/utils/openGraph.ts draws cards with no image dependencies: the
  public-domain 6x10 Misc-Fixed font, NELA's dark palette, an indexed
  PNG written with zlib, and a small LRU.
